     "text": "{\"count\": 3, \"rationale\": \"The target is an OR of three routes (h4_0:access, h4_1:traverse, h4_2:reach), so all three must be cut. Blocking h4_0, h4_1 and h4_2 does this, so 3 blocks are enough. Two blocks cannot work. To cut h4_0 you must block h4_0 itself, or both h2_1 and h2_2, because h2_1 is fed directly by edge0. Blocking h2_1 and h2_2 cuts h4_0 and h4_2, but h4_1 stays reachable through h2_0 (via h1_2). Blocking h4_0 leaves one block, and no single step cuts both h4_1 and h4_2. For example, blocking h1_0 cuts h4_2 and h2_2, but h4_1 stays reachable via h1_2 -> h2_0. So the minimum is 3.\"}"
    }
